{"metadata":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Treap","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"struct","roleHeading":"Structure","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Treap"}],"externalID":"s:17BinarySearchTrees5TreapV","modules":[{"name":"BinarySearchTrees"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"Treap.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/GrafluentCollections\/blob\/main\/Sources\/BinarySearchTrees\/Treap.swift#L31"},"role":"symbol","title":"Treap"},"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/SK","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/Sl","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/Se","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/SE","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/SQ","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s25ExpressibleByArrayLiteralP","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/SH","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/Sk","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/ST","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/s10SetAlgebraP"]}],"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Sorted-sets","generated":true,"title":"Sorted sets","identifiers":["doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/AVLTree","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/RedBlackTree","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/SplayTree"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Treap"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Element"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Element"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SL","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Comparable"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The random priorities make the shape that of a random binary search tree, whatever order the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elements arrive in, so lookup, insertion and removal take O(log "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":") expected time. A treap"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"also splits at an element into the elements below it and the rest, and joins two treaps whose"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elements don’t interleave. The elements are a random-access collection in ascending order,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"indexed by rank like an array: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"treap[0]"},{"type":"text","text":" is the smallest element. Reading an element by index"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"costs O(log "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":") expected, and a pass through the whole collection costs O("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["var numbers: Treap = [8, 3, 5, 1, 9]","let parts = numbers.split(at: 5)","Array(parts.lower)            \/\/ [1, 3]","Array(parts.upper)            \/\/ [5, 8, 9]","var rejoined = parts.lower","try rejoined.join(parts.upper)","rejoined == numbers           \/\/ true"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The priorities come from a random number generator given at creation,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"SystemRandomNumberGenerator","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" by default; a seeded generator makes every shape reproducible."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The treap draws one seed from it and keeps its own generator state, so a copy draws the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"priorities as its original."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The vertices live in flat arrays with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int32"},{"type":"text","text":" links, so the treap holds fewer than 2³¹ − 1"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elements, and copying it copies a few arrays only when one copy is mutated."}]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees"]]},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Structures","generated":true,"title":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/Treap\/Split"]},{"anchor":"Initializers","generated":true,"title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/Treap\/init()","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/Treap\/init(_:)","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/Treap\/init(_:using:)","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/Treap\/init(using:)"]},{"anchor":"Instance-Properties","generated":true,"title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/Treap\/height"]},{"anchor":"Instance-Methods","generated":true,"title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/Treap\/contains(_:)","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/Treap\/elements(in:)-1pv5t","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/Treap\/elements(in:)-98uf2","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/Treap\/join(_:)","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTrees\/documentation\/BinarySearchTrees\/Treap\/lowerBound(_:)","doc:\/\/BinarySearchTr